                    {
                        id make-precious-intermediate-retention
                        title "Keep intermediate outputs protected by .PRECIOUS"
                        kind @fix
                        deps (make-intermediate-files make-build-intent-gate)
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T10:08:30.388591494Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Follow-up to completed make-intermediate-files. Owns target-precious-overrides-intermediate and target-precious-pattern-keeps-an-intermediate: explicit and pattern .PRECIOUS declarations prevent deletion even when the file is otherwise intermediate."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T10:11:03.759827479Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "sealed — decomposition asserted complete (nplan seal)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-13T23:15:47.339878201Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-13T23:17:11.767505376Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "GNU Make 4.4.1 characterised against the pristine oracle before anything moved, and the first cell settled the shape.\n\nBeing intermediate and being deleted are two answers, and `.PRECIOUS` gives only the second. `file.c`'s `remove_intermediates` skips a file when `f->precious`, and nothing anywhere clears `f->intermediate` on its account. The oracle agrees, and the pair that shows it is the pattern form against the name form:\n\n  `.PRECIOUS: %.z`     hello.z is kept, and its absence is still excused —\n                       with hello.tsk current and hello.z gone, `make` says\n                       nothing to be done\n  `.PRECIOUS: hello.z` hello.z is kept, and its absence is NOT excused — the\n                       chain rebuilds, because naming a file as any rule's\n                       prerequisite makes it explicitly mentioned\n                       (`expand_deps` sets `is_explicit`), and a mentioned\n                       file was never intermediate in the first place\n\nSo the name form was already right in Ronin, by the accident that kati records every rule's prerequisites in `mentioned` — the special target's included. It is the same answer for the same reason GNU gives, not a coincidence to be tidied away. The pattern form and `.INTERMEDIATE` beside `.PRECIOUS` are the two the markers owned, and both were deleting.\n\nThe rest of the matrix, all measured:\n\n  base chain              deleted, `rm hello.z` echoed at the end of the build\n  .INTERMEDIATE: name     deleted\n  .SECONDARY: name        kept, absence excused\n  .SECONDARY: (bare)      kept — and see make-bare-secondary-still-builds\n  .NOTINTERMEDIATE: name  kept, absence NOT excused, chain rebuilds\n  .PRECIOUS: %.z on a file an explicit rule made      deleted\n  .PRECIOUS: hello.% against a file named hello.z     deleted\n  .PRECIOUS: %.mid on a `.in.mid:` suffix rule        kept\n  two intermediates       one line, `rm hello.y hello.z`\n  -n                      prints the `rm` it would do, deletes nothing\n  a downstream failure    still sweeps up; `.PRECIOUS` still protects\n  the intermediate's own recipe fails                 swept up; `.PRECIOUS`\n                          protects, .DELETE_ON_ERROR notwithstanding\n\nThe pattern-literal reading dispatch #6 established for `.DELETE_ON_ERROR` transfers exactly: `.PRECIOUS: %.z` protects a name only when the rule that made it has that literal string as its target pattern, which is `implicit.c` looking up `rule->targets[matches]` as a file and copying its `precious` bit. `hello.%` matching `hello.z` protects nothing; a suffix rule does get protection, because kati rewrites `.in.mid:` to the target pattern `%.mid` exactly as GNU does.\n\nThe change is four lines of decision in kati and nothing in Ronin. `keep_precious_intermediates` runs beside `mark_delete_on_error` once the graph is planned, and clears `is_disposable` where `is_precious` says so. It has to wait for the same reason that one does — a pattern protects a name only from the moment the rule that makes it has been chosen — and it reads `recipe_output` beside `output_pattern` for the same reason too: the rule's target pattern speaks for the name the search matched it against and for no other. Deliberately it does not touch `is_intermediate`, which is the whole finding above.\n\nNothing in the retention decision reads a recipe, so the lazy recipe expansion that landed in dispatch #13 cannot reach it.\n\nMarkers. Both owned markers are gone: target-precious-overrides-intermediate and target-precious-pattern-keeps-an-intermediate now match.\n\nFixtures, five recorded from the oracle: target-intermediate-kept-by-a-precious-pattern, target-precious-pattern-keeps-a-suffix-rule-intermediate, target-precious-pattern-keeps-an-intermediate-after-a-failure, target-precious-pattern-does-not-match-an-intermediate-name, target-precious-pattern-ignores-an-explicitly-made-intermediate. The last two are the negatives, and they are what make the pattern-literal reading a claim rather than a coincidence. One Ronin test, `a_precious_pattern_keeps_an_intermediate_in_the_direct_graph`, asserts both halves separately on the compiled graph — protected and still intermediate — with an unprotected sibling as the control, and says out loud that a parsed manifest carries neither.\n\nThree defects found and left as follow-ups under make-subsumption rather than folded in, each with a recorded reproducer carrying a divergence marker: make-bare-secondary-still-builds, make-pattern-peer-is-not-intermediate, make-pattern-peer-restart-convergence."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-13T23:17:28.786122174Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Gates, all run under scripts/sandboxed.\n\n  cargo fmt --all --check                        clean\n  cargo check --workspace --all-targets          clean\n  cargo test --workspace                         744 passed, 743 at baseline;\n                                                 the one addition is this\n                                                 node's equivalence test\n  cargo test --workspace --all-targets           784 passed, 1 ignored, 0 failed\n  clippy, ronin lib+bins --no-deps, pedantic\n    and nursery                                  clean\n  clippy -p kati --all-targets -D warnings       clean\n  Make build-intent oracle                       422 gating cases, 415 at\n                                                 baseline; the seven added are\n                                                 five for this node and two\n                                                 reproducers for follow-ups\n  scripts/check-make-conformance.sh              387 runs, 309 identical /\n                                                 78 differing — the baseline\n                                                 exactly\n  scripts/check-make-equivalence.sh              297 makefiles, 276 graphs\n                                                 compared, 0 disagreements\n  scripts/check-make-upstream.sh                 1287 rows, unclassified 504 /\n                                                 compiler 37 / interface 46 /\n                                                 narration 700 — every count\n                                                 the baseline's\n\nThe combined Clippy line in scripts/check-release.sh is red as it was before, on examples and tests this change does not touch; the two findings it reports in src/make/equivalence.rs are on `Case::both`, which predates this node.\n\nThe upstream inventory reports one moved row and it is not this change's. `features/patternrules.diff.34` reads `ninja-progress+no-work-line+up-to-date-line+evaluation` in the record and `ninja-progress+product-name+up-to-date-line+evaluation` on a fresh run. Two proofs it is not ours: the full gate reproduces exactly that drift with the kati change stashed, and four focused runs of the same suite file against one binary produced `ronin: no work to do.` twice and `ronin: manifest ... dirty after 100 tries` twice. It is a second flapper beside the known features/reinvoke.diff.2, and it now has a deterministic reproducer and a node — make-pattern-peer-restart-convergence. The recorded row is left as it stands rather than re-recorded, because recording one face of a flap makes the next dispatch see it flap back.\n\nThe `rm hello.z` narration GNU prints when it sweeps up is still not printed, and this node does not owe it: src/make/report.rs says so where it discards them, for the reason make.narration+1 gives — Make mode narrates in the manifest front end's shape. It is unchanged by this work either way."
                            }

