                text "Implemented deferred shell command substitution for statically classified recursive Make invocations. The direct graph sink now carries the recipe shell and flags to the child resolver; substitutions execute only after the parent-prerequisite evaluation boundary, in the recipe directory and compiled environment, then undergo quoted/unquoted shell word handling before Make argv parsing. Two regressions cover a Zstd-shaped pipeline assignment and a substitution that must read a prerequisite-generated file. The retained Zstd tree now computes conf_b7fa5eb4cb1f6c5f21930f5277aefbd8 and gets past the original static-invocation refusal. It then exposes a distinct Kati substitution-reference defect: debug.c becomes debug.o.o through $(SRC:.c=.o) / $(OBJ0:.S=.o); filed as make-substitution-reference-suffix. Full workspace tests pass, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy passes, and the Make regression suite passes."
            }

